# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-28, with the injection applied:
#   two green probes (t+4s, t+9s), then the daemon stopped answering 15s into
#   its life while its process stayed up — TASK-Q07Y5's production symptom.
exit: 1

# The window opened, so the soak got a booted, serving, healthy daemon first.
# Without this line the artifact would also accept a soak that failed at boot,
# which proves nothing about uptime.
contains: [soak] holding the daemon

# The finding is about the daemon, not about the harness around it.
contains: SOAK FAIL: the daemon

# Two legitimate shapes of the same defect, decided by whether `serve` is still
# parked on its signal wait when the drain budget expires (it usually is, which
# is why the operator saw a live process serving nobody) or has already
# unwound. Either is the daemon taking itself out of service unasked.
contains-any: stopped answering
contains-any: exited on its own
